 CBArgsFireWinIni msg;WINI;r
⍝ DemoCallbackArgs: deliver Root's WinIniChange through a real ⎕DQ - what a
⍝ Windows settings broadcast (resuming from sleep, say) does - and report
⍝ whether the callback bound through eWS ran and the ⎕DQ survived.
⍝ ⎕NQ stands in for the broadcast; a native Timer ends the ⎕DQ.
⍝ A callback bound in the wrong namespace makes ⎕DQ signal VALUE ERROR.
 WINI←0 ⍝ Set by CBArgsWinIni, which runs on top of this ⎕DQ
 :Trap 0
     '.'eWS'Event' 'WinIniChange' 'CBArgsWinIni'
     'WINITIMER'⎕WC'Timer'('Interval' 300)('Event' 'Timer' 1)
     ⎕NQ'.' 'WinIniChange'
     {}⎕DQ'WINITIMER'
     r←(1+WINI)⊃'callback did not run' 'callback ran, ⎕DQ survived'
 :Else
     r←'⎕DQ failed: ',⎕DMX.EM
 :EndTrap
 ⎕EX'WINITIMER'
 '.'eWS'Event' 'WinIniChange' 0 ⍝ Leave Root as we found it
 'F1.OUT'eWS'Caption'('WinIniChange: ',r)
